From 02beaa9040c47f489991bac14c0bdc00b7a737c9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jakub Skokan <jakub.skokan@havefun.cz>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 23:58:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] NFS: drain server sysfs before releasing client state v2

The per-server shutdown attribute accesses the server's RPC clients and
shared nfs_client. nfs_free_server() released those clients before removing
the sysfs object, allowing a concurrent shutdown_store() to use freed state
during final unmount.

NFSv2/v3 initialization has the same lifetime requirement. It publishes the
server sysfs object before starting lockd and creating the main RPC client,
but its error path cleared and put server->nfs_client before common
teardown. An admitted sysfs callback could therefore observe NULL or freed
shared-client state. In all publication paths, the main RPC client can also
retain its initial error-pointer value while the shutdown attribute is
live.

Withdraw the sysfs object and drain active callbacks before list removal,
destroy callbacks, RPC shutdown, or the shared-client put. Once
nfs_get_client() assigns server->nfs_client, retain that sole reference
through later initialization failures and let nfs_free_server() release it
after the drain. Treat NULL and error-valued RPC client pointers as
unavailable in the common shutdown helper, while continuing to cancel every
valid main, ACL, NLM, and shared client. Keep the final guarded
kobject_put() late and preserve the existing destroy, list, and
unpublished-kobject guards.

This changes callback lifetime ordering and partial-initialization handling
only. The sysfs ABI, NFS wire behavior, client sharing, and successful
mount/unmount behavior remain unchanged. The patch is an independent fix
against v6.12.116; reviewed v1 source is preserved at commit 94b072af9c09
("NFS: drain sysfs callbacks before destroying server clients") and no
upstream status is claimed.

Development history:
- v1: Withdraw and drain the per-server sysfs object before destroying
  callback state during normal teardown.
- v2: Retain the NFSv2/v3 client reference through post-publication
  initialization failures so common teardown drains callbacks before
  release, and make shutdown ignore an absent/error main RPC clone in every
  publication path while continuing to cancel the valid shared client.

Fixes: d9615d166c7e ("NFS: add sysfs shutdown knob")
Signed-off-by: Jakub Skokan <jakub.skokan@havefun.cz>
---
 fs/nfs/client.c | 10 +++++-----
 fs/nfs/sysfs.c  |  4 ++--
 2 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/fs/nfs/client.c b/fs/nfs/client.c
index bb3f882d8c24..6c6a3d9da487 100644
--- a/fs/nfs/client.c
+++ b/fs/nfs/client.c
@@ -826,8 +826,6 @@ static int nfs_init_server(struct nfs_server *server,
 	return 0;
 
 error:
-	server->nfs_client = NULL;
-	nfs_put_client(clp);
 	return error;
 }
 
@@ -1098,6 +1096,10 @@ static void delayed_free(struct rcu_head *p)
  */
 void nfs_free_server(struct nfs_server *server)
 {
+	/* Drain sysfs callbacks before destroying the clients they access. */
+	if (server->kobj.state_initialized)
+		nfs_sysfs_remove_server(server);
+
 	nfs_server_remove_lists(server);
 
 	if (server->destroy != NULL)
@@ -1110,10 +1112,8 @@ void nfs_free_server(struct nfs_server *server)
 
 	nfs_put_client(server->nfs_client);
 
-	if (server->kobj.state_initialized) {
-		nfs_sysfs_remove_server(server);
+	if (server->kobj.state_initialized)
 		kobject_put(&server->kobj);
-	}
 	ida_free(&s_sysfs_ids, server->s_sysfs_id);
 
 	put_cred(server->cred);
diff --git a/fs/nfs/sysfs.c b/fs/nfs/sysfs.c
index f9e6c8340929..1a9abeed5e69 100644
--- a/fs/nfs/sysfs.c
+++ b/fs/nfs/sysfs.c
@@ -226,8 +226,8 @@ static bool shutdown_match_client(const struct rpc_task *task, const void *data)
 
 static void shutdown_client(struct rpc_clnt *clnt)
 {
-	/* There is nothing to cancel if the client is absent. */
-	if (!clnt)
+	/* There is nothing to cancel if the client is absent or unavailable. */
+	if (IS_ERR_OR_NULL(clnt))
 		return;
 	clnt->cl_shutdown = 1;
 	rpc_cancel_tasks(clnt, -EIO, shutdown_match_client, NULL);
